am initial_state: The initial quantum state vector.\n606-    :type initial_state: Tensor\n607-    :param times: Time points for which to compute the evolution. Should be a 1D array of times.\n608-    :type times: Tensor\n609-    :param callback: Optional function to apply to the state at each time step.\n610-    :type callback: Optional[Callable[..., Tensor]]\n611-    :param args: Additional arguments to pass to the Hamiltonian function.\n612-    :type args: tuple | list\n613-    :param solver_kws: Additional keyword arguments to pass to the ODE solver.\n614-\n615-        - ``ode_backend='jaxode'`` (default) uses ``jax.experimental.ode.odeint``; ``ode_backend='diffrax'``\n616-          uses ``diffrax.diffeqsolve``.\n617-\n618-        - ``rtol`` (default: 1e-8) and ``atol`` (default: 1e-8) are used to determine how accurately you would\n619-          like the numerical approximation to your equation.\n620-\n621-        - The ``solver`` parameter accepts one of {'Tsit5' (default), 'Dopri5', 'Dopri8', 'Kvaerno5'}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
