{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_73","type":"agent_message","text":"The solution is complete and passes every criterion. Final summary:\n\n**What was built:** `/root/solution_6.py` with `run_solution(config)`, at 146 non-empty/non-comment lines, no print statements, pure framework-native computation on the JAX backend of TensorCircuit-NG.\n\n**Implementation:**\n- **Analog blocks:** each block evolves the state under `H_analog = J·Σ(XX+YY) + Δ·Σ(−1)ⁱZ` via `tc.timeevol.ode_evol_global` — TensorCircuit's continuous-time Schrödinger ODE engine, backed by `jax.experimental.ode.odeint` (Dopri5), with `rtol`/`atol` passed as the config tolerances and `max_steps=16` as the integrator step bound. The sparse Hamiltonians are built once as JAX `BCOO` matrices and combined per-block from the trainable couplings.\n- **Digital blocks:** each qubit gets the exact single-qubit equivalent of `RZ(α)·RY(β)·RZ(γ)` (a combined 2×2 unitary applied through `c.apply_general_gate`, verified bit-for-bit against the three-gate circuit — this was essential, since the three separate gate applications made backward compilation ~3× slower).\n- **Training:** exact gradients via `jax.value_and_grad` through the ODE, gates, and measurements; hand-rolled Adam at lr 0.12 for exactly 100 steps; energy density `<H_target>/14` measured with `tc.expectation` over all 53 Pauli terms, recorded before each update.\n\n**Verified results (default config):**\n- Total wall time: **55.5 s** (well under the 180 s/300 s limits)\n- History length 100; initial −0.6324 → final **−1.2779** energy density\n- Exact sparse ground-state density (via eigsh, checked offline): −1.6026 — final is above it within tolerance and comfortably within 1.0\n- Times `[0.138, 0.136, 0.262, 0.303]` ∈ (0.05, 0.50); couplings and detunings all ∈ (−1, 1); shapes `(4,)`\n- All returned values are NumPy arrays with exactly the four required keys"}}
